window.docContents[2].resolve({"/Proof-of-Iwasawa-theorem/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--Proof-of-Iwasawa-theorem":{"contents":"This chapter proves Iwasawa's theorem, namely that the Coleman map induces an\nisomorphism of -modules\n\nThe strategy has four movements. First we put a -module structure on\nthe norm-coherent local units  and show the Coleman map is\nequivariant for it. Next we compute the kernel and cokernel of the Coleman map by\nanalysing each constituent map; this is the fundamental exact sequence. Then we\nexhibit explicit cyclic generators of the global and local cyclotomic units over\nthe relevant group rings. Finally we feed the generators through the Coleman map\nto read off the image of the cyclotomic units, and conclude.\n\nThroughout,  is an odd prime, ,\n via the cyclotomic character , and\n is the quotient by complex conjugation. We write\n,  for a uniformiser,  for\nthe local units of ,  for those congruent to  modulo\n, and ,\n for the norm-coherent towers. Recall\nthe Coleman map is the composition\n\nwhere  is the Mahler transform identifying measures with power series.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"An introduction to p-adic L-functions — Lean blueprint","header":"11. Proof of Iwasawa theorem","id":"/Proof-of-Iwasawa-theorem/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--Proof-of-Iwasawa-theorem"}});